{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"## The Fundamental Theorem of Calculus\n\nIf $~\\displaystyle g(x)=\\int_a^xf(t)\\,dt\\,$, then $~g^\\prime (x)=f(x)\\,$\n\nThis only works if $f$ is continuous on $[a,b]$.\n\nThankfully, the function $f(t) = \\dfrac{1}{{1 + {t^{\\,3}}}}$ is continuous on $[2,2]$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"## Applying the theorem\n\nWe're given:\n\n$\\displaystyle g(x) = \\int_{2}^{x} {\\frac{1}{{1 + {t^{\\,3}}}}\\,dt} $\n\nSo the theorem tells us:\n\n$\\displaystyle g\\,^\\prime(x) = \\frac{1}{{1 + {x^{\\,3}}}} $\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"## Evaluating $g'\\left(2\\right)$\n\n$\\displaystyle g\\,^\\prime(2) = \\frac{1}{{1 + 2^3}}=\\dfrac{1}{9}$\n\nThe answer:\n\n$g'\\left(2\\right)=\\dfrac19$\n","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$\\displaystyle g(x) = \\int_{2}^{x} {\\frac{1}{{1 + {t^{\\,3}}}}\\,dt} \\,$\n\n$\\displaystyle g\\,^\\prime(2)\\, =$\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{-7}{18}$","correct":false},{"content":"$0$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1}{9}$","correct":true},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1}{3}$","correct":false},{"content":"None of these","correct":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
